menu "FIDO authenticator"

config FIDO_TEST_AUTO_UP
    bool "TEST ONLY: grant user presence without a button press"
    default n
    help
      Makes every FIDO touch check succeed immediately. Used only by the
      host test script on a board with no BOOT button press available.
      Never enable this in a shipped firmware.

endmenu

menu "Development"

config DEV_BACKDOOR
    bool "DEV ONLY: touchless reflash and log access over USB"
    default n
    help
      Development convenience. Enables:
        - vendor CTAPHID 0x51 entering ROM download mode without a BOOT press,
        - vendor CTAPHID 0x52 (read the firmware log over FIDO HID),
        - POST /api/reboot?mode=download without a BOOT press.
      Anyone with USB access can then reflash the device without touching it.
      Never ship a firmware with this enabled. Release builds leave it off (download mode then needs BOOT held 3 s);
      dev builds add it via sdkconfig.dev.

config DEV_AUTORECOVER
    bool "DEV ONLY: reboot into ROM download mode if no HTTP request in 60 s"
    depends on DEV_BACKDOOR
    default n
    help
      If no HTTP request has been served within 60 s of boot, the firmware
      reboots into ROM download mode so it can be reflashed without anyone
      pressing BOOT. A board that is simply unplugged from a host will also
      drop into download mode. Must be off for a shipping build.

endmenu
